save(79,dict(paragraphs=["Gourhari Das writes across poetry, short fiction, novels, essays and drama, and translates into Odia. His short-story collection Kanta O Anyanya Galpa received the Sahitya Akademi Award in 2012. His Odia translation of Benyamin’s Goat Days, Chheli Chareibara Dina, received the Akademi’s translation award for 2021. The Labyrinth brings his fiction to English readers in Manoranjan Mishra’s translation.","His poem ‘ଗୋଟେ ସମୟରେ, ଏଇ ପୃଥିବୀରେ’ gives love a quieter measure than reunion. Through flowers, remembered roads and the distance between two lives, it finds value in having shared a time on earth. Its returning phrases hold that recognition gently, even when society and circumstance keep the lovers apart."],sources=[source('Sahitya Akademi — Odia award winners','https://sahitya-akademi.gov.in/awards/akademi%20samman_suchi.jsp',['2012 award; Kanta O Anyanya Galpa']),source('Sahitya Akademi — translation awards','https://sahitya-akademi.gov.in/awards/anuvad_samman_suchi.jsp',['2021 award; Chheli Chareibara Dina; Benyamin original']),source('The Labyrinth — Niyogi Books','https://niyogibooksindia.com/books/the-labyrinth/',['Author genre range; English novel translated by Manoranjan Mishra'])],books=[dict(title='The Labyrinth',detail='Novel · translated from Odia by Manoranjan Mishra · Niyogi Books',url='https://niyogibooksindia.com/books/the-labyrinth/')],identity_match='Odia author identity, genre range and both Akademi awards match captured biography. External sources spell first name Gourahari; site display name preserved.',poems_read=[dict(id=101,title='ଗୋଟେ ସମୟରେ, ଏଇ ପୃଥିବୀରେ',basis='Full Odia original read: shared earthly time, social judgment, remembered roads, recurring flowers and distant lovers.')],limitations=['Secondary newspaper article incorrectly attributes Goat Days to Uday Prakash; official Akademi identifies Benyamin and is used instead.','Award year 2021 distinguished from announcement in 2022.','Book publication year omitted: publisher advance sheet has inconsistent date presentation.','No inference that lyric lovers represent the author’s personal relationships.'],next_action='Independent editor to review transliteration and prose.'))
